# Gangamata Transport — Frontend Environment Variables (Example)
# Copy to .env and adjust as needed. Never commit .env.

# API Base URL — the one backend shared by the office console and the driver app (NestJS on
# Render, data in Supabase PostgreSQL). Production builds (`npm run build`, i.e. Vercel) already get
# it from the committed .env.production, so the live console can never fall back to demo data.
# Copy this for `npm run dev` to work against the same API.
# Unset only for the self-contained prototype demo (`npm run build:demo`), which uses sample data.
VITE_API_URL=https://gtransport-7vgf.onrender.com

# ── Live Fleet map (Phase 6) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Live Fleet draws on MapLibre GL JS, and what it draws is set by a map *style*: a JSON document
# that names the tile source. The style is configuration, not code, so pointing a deployment at a
# self-hosted OpenStreetMap-derived tile server (or a tile provider you have a production agreement
# with) is an environment change. Use any MapLibre-compatible style URL: an absolute https URL, or
# a root-relative path for a style served from this app's own host.
#
# It is deliberately unset by default and there is no built-in map. Without it the Fleet screen
# says "Map configuration is unavailable." and the driver list, details and Open in Google Maps
# keep working. The value is public (VITE_* variables are embedded in the bundle): if a provider
# needs a key, use its browser-safe, domain-restricted kind. A private server key never belongs here.
#
# Local development only: OpenFreeMap serves OpenStreetMap data through a public style with no
# key. Do not use it, or the public openstreetmap.org tile servers, as the production source.
# VITE_MAP_STYLE_URL=https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty
